Package: statnnet
Title: Statistical Selection and Interpretation for Neural Networks Fitted with 'nnet'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Andrew", "McInerney", , "andrew.mcinerney@ul.ie", role = c("aut",
    "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2348-2159")),
    person("Kevin", "Burke", , "kevin.burke@ul.ie", role = "aut")
  )
Author: Andrew McInerney [aut, cre, cph] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2348-2159>),
    Kevin Burke [aut]
Maintainer: Andrew McInerney <andrew.mcinerney@ul.ie>
Description: Provides statistically based selection and interpretation for
    small, single-hidden-layer neural networks fitted with 'nnet'. The package
    implements information-criterion selection of inputs and hidden-layer size,
    validates fitted models, reconstructs their objectives and curvature,
    estimates penalised sandwich covariance matrices, provides individual and
    grouped Wald-type diagnostics, and calculates predictive finite-difference
    and partial-dependence covariate effects with uncertainty. Methods follow
    McInerney and Burke (2025) <doi:10.1177/1471082X241258261> and McInerney
    and Burke (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2311.08139>.
